mod:free_container_storage;
// 2026-11-15 (landing 177d2b7, row 1: DEF-660's K-a2 as V1 with F6). A FREE OF STORAGE A CONTAINER OWNS IS REFUSED AT THE FREE. `dalloc`, `ralloc` and `wildx_free`
// handed a pointer that may point into storage a `List`, slice, string, cstring or buffer names are BORROW-011 at the call: the container frees that storage
// again at its drop. The argument is followed under its casts, `raw`, `relay` and `move`, into a ternary's and a `??`'s arms and a local's initialiser, to a
// header's spelled `.ptr`, then by the refs its value carries; a string's, cstring's or buffer's `.ptr` carries its header's address. A header over the
// program's own `wild` storage is no container: a `wild` slice, a `wild` header that isn't a local, or a local made by `#wild_slice<T>(p, n)` over a `wild`
// pointer; a `wild` string, cstring or buffer local still owns its buffer, so it is one. A ternary's or a `??`'s arm spends one of eight and a copy one of 64,
// and each end refuses. A callee that frees through a parameter's own value (`pfrees`, an impl's joined into its trait method's) is asked at its call. One
// cell a face, its names suffixed with the cell's. Each face is accepted by main (78f9b3a) and frees twice or frees what it doesn't own there (74 at -O0 and
// -O2, 97 under the detector, or another fault exit); each is refused by this row. The right controls are in `free_container_storage_ok.npk` and
// `free_container_storage_attack_ok.npk`.
// THE FACES, by their first parts: the in-frame frees of an element, a range's `.ptr` and a header's `.ptr` (`dr_`, `b_`, `ix_`, `sp_`, `sc_`, `sl_`, `rt_`,
// `mv_`, `cp_`, `us_`, `kc_`); through a field, an assignment, an array slot, a ternary, a `??`, a getter, a holder, a view, a callee's result (`bd_`, `gt_`,
// `gn_`, `hb_`, `hs_`, `hl_`, `if_`, `ls_`, `nl_`, `wsx_`, `ca40_`, `wh_`, `ec_`, `sa_`, `as_`, `fa_`); through a callee that frees (`f3_`..`f6_`, `fr_`, `fs_`,
// `mw_`, `mr_`, `cs_`, `tc_`), through a trait's method (`tg_`, `tg2_`); a buffer's `.ptr` (`bf_`); the string roads (`pa_`, `pk2_`, `pke_`, `pb1_`..`pd5_`); and
// the `List` ranges that must stay refused beside R1 (`pf1_`..`pf9_`). From the attack on the row (`Ailp-team_146`) and its checkpoint: the `.ptr` of a header
// no place holds (a call's result) or of a parameter, reached through a local, a ternary's arm or a getter (`tp_`, `pr_`, `ps_`, `dc_`, `gp_`), a holder reached
// from two holders (`hc_two`), a `wild` string, cstring or buffer local's `.ptr` (`wsx_str`, `wsx_cp`, `wsx_fld`, `wsx_tn`, `wbx_buf`), a string's
// `.ptr` reached through a pointer parameter, a pointer local or `self` (`sp_`; alone, each runs 67 on main only because `exit` drops nothing), and the walk's ends:
// a ternary or a `??` nine deep, sixty-odd casts and a mix of the two (`tc63`, `tc70`, `fu_`).
// THE PRICES, each a right program this row refuses, named here and not tested: a later re-point or assignment that does not clear an earlier ref (`kp_reas_ok`,
// `bd_strasg_c`, `pb6_holdw_ok`, `ph_ok`; at parity with main's `kq_reas_ok`, `kq_later_ok` and `ph_tw`); the getter's result (`gp_loc_ok`, `gs_ok`, `gw_ok`,
// `ws_get_ok`, `gp_x2_c`, `gt_a_c`; at parity with main's `gp_tw_ok`); a copy out of a slice (`ws_sl2_ok`; main's `sl_blk_ok`); the 32nd parameter (`an32_ok`;
// main's `an32_tw_ok`); a callee's second free (`sf_two_ok`; main's `sf_two_tw`); a window at a move or an eat (`pw_mv_ok`, `pw_eat_ok`; main's `pw_mv_tw` and
// `pw_eat_tw`); and, off parity: R1's five (`pe1_wsub_ok`, `pe2_wsubl_ok`, `wsl_ix_ok`, `wsl_fld_ok`, `pf4_wsl2_ok`: a slice over the program's own `wild`
// block reached through a range, an element or a field), eight or more nested arms (`tn8_ok`, `fu_tn9_ok`), a `wild` place's refs per holder (`kp_fldv_ok`,
// `pa9_fldv8_ok`, `kp_cp_ok`, `nv_cp_ok`, `nv2_ok`, `vp2_ok`, `kp_blk_tw0_ok`, `hc_two_ok`) and the window class (`pw_mv_x_ok`, `pz_push_ok`, `pz_ret_ok`),
// each its LOW number; `tp_tn_c` and `cf_ok` are the row's rule (a container's storage handed to a callee or an arm that may free it).
error:E5;
struct:K_b_dal = { int64:k; };
func:mk_b_dal = List<int64>() never fails { List<int64>:l = raw list_init::<int64>(2i64); drop list_push(@l, 1i64); drop list_push(@l, 2i64); pass l; };
func:growl_b_dal = int64(List<int64>->:l) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
func:g_b_dal = int64(int64:n) never fails {
    List<int64>:l = raw mk_b_dal();
    int64->:e = @l[0i64];
    dalloc((l[0i64...1i64].ptr) =>! wild any->);
    pass (<-e) + 6i64;
};
func:f_b_dal = int64(int64:n) never fails { pass raw g_b_dal(n); };
func:cell_main_b_dal = int32() never fails { pass (((raw f_b_dal(1i64)) + 60i64) =>! int32); };
struct:K_b_ral = { int64:k; };
func:mk_b_ral = List<int64>() never fails { List<int64>:l = raw list_init::<int64>(2i64); drop list_push(@l, 1i64); drop list_push(@l, 2i64); pass l; };
func:growl_b_ral = int64(List<int64>->:l) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
func:g_b_ral = int64(int64:n) never fails {
    List<int64>:l = raw mk_b_ral();
    int64->:e = @l[0i64];
    wild int8->:q = ralloc((l[0i64...1i64].ptr) =>! wild any->, 4096i64);
    pass (<-e) + 6i64;
};
func:f_b_ral = int64(int64:n) never fails { pass raw g_b_ral(n); };
func:cell_main_b_ral = int32() never fails { pass (((raw f_b_ral(1i64)) + 60i64) =>! int32); };
